invariant: INV-16
file: src/rsa_sign64_blind.h
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: blinded_exponents blinds dq with r_p in place of r_q, so the
  last 8 bytes of the blind are never read and the two halves share one
  r. Every signature is still the same bytes. bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test
  holds dq's exponent to the one r_q gives.

--- old
    blinded_prime_exponent(e_q, k->dq, k->q, half_len, blind + BLIND_R_LEN);
--- new
    blinded_prime_exponent(e_q, k->dq, k->q, half_len, blind);
